          "ratio": "1:1"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Anton started out cutting his friends' hair. A friend's haircut is never really about the hair — he already knew what to cut. It was about the half hour of talking, every time a continuation, not awkward small talk about nothing."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "items": [
        {
          "type": "image",
          "image": "/images/ser 17-1.png",
          "ratio": "1:1"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Servant is *serve* and *ant* together: to serve, and Anton. The name holds both at once — the work itself, and the person doing it."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "items": [
        {
          "type": "image",
          "image": "/images/ser 4-1.png",
          "ratio": "3:4"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "image": "/images/ser 2-2.png",
          "ratio": "3:4"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "\"So where were we?\" — the line Anton opens with when someone he knows sits down again. It works two ways at once: the hair, and the last thing you talked about. That line became the whole brand."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "items": [
        {
          "type": "image",
          "image": "/images/ser 21.png",
          "ratio": "4:3"
        },
        {
          "type": "break"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "image": "/images/ser 15-4.png",
          "ratio": "1:1"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "image": "/images/ser 13.png",
          "ratio": "1:1"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "A classic barbershop serif — the vocabulary of a real trade, not a new arrival. It doesn't read as a master showing off, but as a sign of a place that has been here long enough to know everyone."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "items": [
        {
          "type": "image",
          "image": "/images/ser 18-1.png",
          "ratio": "4:3"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Warm brown belongs to things that age well — leather, wood, coffee, an old photograph. A place that stays and remembers everyone should be the color of what time improves, not what came new out of a box."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "items": [
        {
          "type": "image",
          "image": "/images/ser 20.png",
          "ratio": "4:3"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The line lives wherever Anton speaks to a client — in a booking reminder, on the mirror, on the card. Not a slogan, just the way he actually talks."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "items": [
        {
          "type": "image",
          "image": "/images/ser 19-1.png",
          "ratio": "4:3"
        },
        {
          "type": "break"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "image": "/images/ser 22.png",
          "ratio": "1:1"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "image": "/images/ChatGPT Image Aug 1 2026 (15)-1.png",
          "ratio": "1:1"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Servant didn't invent a value, it kept one: cut a client the way you'd cut a friend, without starting from zero. Everything else — the mark, the color, the words — just holds that in place."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
